# Highport Environment Variables

This file is an **overview index**. Each app has its own `.env.example` with full documentation and per-variable comments. For local development, copy each app's example into place:

```bash
cp apps/web/.env.example       apps/web/.env
cp apps/server/.env.example    apps/server/.env
cp apps/rag-service/.env.example apps/rag-service/.env

# Then generate the NextAuth secret (required by apps/web):
npx auth secret >> apps/web/.env
```

After copying, edit each `.env` file to fill in real values. The web `.env` requires at minimum `AUTH_SECRET`; the server `.env` requires at minimum `DATABASE_URL`. The RAG service is optional — leave its defaults to use local Ollama + ChromaDB, or follow [docs/rag-setup.md](./docs/rag-setup.md) for the full AI setup.

## Variable Overview

| Variable                       | App      | Required | Purpose                                              |
| ------------------------------ | -------- | -------- | ---------------------------------------------------- |
| `AUTH_SECRET`                  | web      | yes      | NextAuth JWT signing secret (`npx auth secret`)        |
| `NEXT_PUBLIC_WS_URL`           | web      | yes      | Hocuspocus WebSocket URL (e.g. `ws://localhost:18121`) |
| `NEXT_PUBLIC_API_URL`          | web      | yes      | Fastify REST API URL (e.g. `http://localhost:18122`)   |
| `NEXT_PUBLIC_RAG_URL`          | web      | optional | RAG service URL — leave unset to disable AI chat      |
| `NEXT_PUBLIC_RAG_SERVICE_URL`  | web      | optional | Alternate RAG URL used by chargen features            |
| `NEXT_PUBLIC_SERVER_URL`       | web      | optional | Server URL for portrait/conflict features             |
| `DATABASE_URL`                 | server   | yes      | PostgreSQL connection string                          |
| `RAG_SERVICE_URL`              | server   | optional | RAG service URL (portrait generation)                |
| `PORTRAIT_STORAGE_TYPE`        | server   | optional | `local` (default) or `s3`                            |
| `PORTRAIT_STORAGE_PATH`        | server   | optional | Local filesystem path for portraits                  |
| `PORTRAIT_S3_BUCKET`           | server   | optional | Required if `PORTRAIT_STORAGE_TYPE=s3`               |
| `AWS_ACCESS_KEY_ID`            | server   | optional | Required if `PORTRAIT_STORAGE_TYPE=s3`               |
| `AWS_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY`        | server   | optional | Required if `PORTRAIT_STORAGE_TYPE=s3`               |
| `LLM_PROVIDER`                 | rag-svc  | yes      | `ollama` (default, local) or `gemini` (cloud)        |
| `VECTORDB_PROVIDER`            | rag-svc  | yes      | `chroma` (default, local) or `pinecone` (cloud)      |
| `OLLAMA_BASE_URL`              | rag-svc  | optional | Ollama server URL (default `http://localhost:11434`) |
| `GEMINI_API_KEY`               | rag-svc  | optional | Required if `LLM_PROVIDER=gemini`                   |
| `PINECONE_API_KEY`             | rag-svc  | optional | Required if `VECTORDB_PROVIDER=pinecone`            |
| `PINECONE_INDEX_NAME`          | rag-svc  | optional | Required if `VECTORDB_PROVIDER=pinecone`            |
| `PINECONE_ENVIRONMENT`         | rag-svc  | optional | Required if `VECTORDB_PROVIDER=pinecone`            |

## Deployment

For Vercel (frontend) and external backend hosting, see [DEPLOYMENT.md](./DEPLOYMENT.md). Production secrets belong in your hosting provider's environment variable settings — **never commit `.env` files**.
